@startuml
title Writer - Note Lifecycle

[*] --> Active : Create note

Active --> Archived : Archive
Archived --> Active : Unarchive

Active --> Trash : Move to trash
Archived --> Trash : Move to trash

Trash --> Active : Restore [previously active]
Trash --> Archived : Restore [previously archived]

Trash --> PermanentlyDeleted : Permanently delete
PermanentlyDeleted --> [*]

note right of Active
  Lifecycle summary:
  Notes can be active, archived,
  or in the trash. Restoring a note
  returns it to its previous active
  or archived state. Permanent deletion
  ends the lifecycle. Favorites are
  independent of these states.
end note
@enduml
